08:17.740 --> 08:22.070
Man, it's reassuring to have 
the Lion Fangs as our escort!

08:22.070 --> 08:24.680
Well, the lord is going with you, too.

08:24.680 --> 08:25.930
Wait, Takumi...

08:25.930 --> 08:27.980
What are you having draw the carriage?

08:28.250 --> 08:30.060
That's amazing!

08:30.060 --> 08:31.770
That's a drake horse, right?

08:32.260 --> 08:33.940
What a splendid carriage.

08:34.380 --> 08:37.320
Lord Godwin! Everyone! Good morning!

08:37.320 --> 08:39.280
I hope we all have a
smooth ride to the capital.

08:39.280 --> 08:43.000
No, no, I'm sorry for adding even 
more trouble to your plate.

08:43.000 --> 08:45.920
Mr. Takumi, may I have a 
look inside the carriage?

08:45.920 --> 08:48.120
Of course, help yourself!

08:49.170 --> 08:51.210
Mr. Takumi!

08:51.570 --> 08:53.940
I-Is something the matter?!

08:53.940 --> 08:55.520
Th-This carriage!

08:55.520 --> 08:57.200
Did you really build it yourself?!

08:57.670 --> 08:59.270
Oh, yes.

08:59.270 --> 09:01.020
Though I did get some 
advice from a blacksmith—

09:01.020 --> 09:03.940
There are so many shocking 
features and functions!

09:03.940 --> 09:05.560
It's truly a bolt out of the blue!

09:05.560 --> 09:08.400
If you wouldn't mind, could you 
please tell me the details?!

09:08.400 --> 09:10.420
Of course, I won't 
ask for them for free!

09:10.420 --> 09:13.180
I'll pay you the proper reward and fees!

09:13.180 --> 09:14.520
Could we please, <i>please</i> carry this—

09:14.780 --> 09:17.010
Would you calm down? That's too much.

09:17.010 --> 09:19.080
You're leaving Mr. Iruma confused.

09:19.080 --> 09:21.640
H-How terribly rude of me.

09:21.640 --> 09:22.240
It's fine.

09:22.550 --> 09:25.370
Still, this truly is a splendid carriage.

09:25.370 --> 09:26.890
Thank you so much.

09:26.890 --> 09:31.810
I would truly be blessed to have 
a carriage like this on hand.

09:31.810 --> 09:35.580
As the lord, I would love to try
traveling in a carriage like this.

09:35.580 --> 09:38.270
Such a splendid carriage.

09:38.270 --> 09:40.580
<i>The lord wants one, doesn't he?</i>

09:40.580 --> 09:43.470
If you could make a carriage 
like this for me,

09:43.470 --> 09:46.780
I wouldn't hesitate to 
pay 100 platinum for it.

09:47.060 --> 09:49.500
<b>Platinum</b>

09:47.390 --> 09:49.400
<i>One hundred platinum...</i>

09:49.360 --> 09:51.520
<b>1,000,000,000 Yen</b>

09:49.360 --> 09:51.520
<b>1,000,000,000 Yen</b>

09:49.400 --> 09:51.070
<i>That's a billion in Japanese yen!</i>

09:52.140 --> 09:55.830
<i>And so, our journey to the 
royal capital, Bakilatos, began.</i>

09:59.440 --> 10:03.690
Mr. Iruma has made great 
contributions to my domain.

10:03.690 --> 10:07.140
Now he's going to play an even greater role,
 become known far and wide,

10:07.140 --> 10:09.660
and soar to even greater heights.

10:09.660 --> 10:11.700
I believe it is as you say.

10:11.700 --> 10:15.620
Though exceptional talent 
attracts all sorts.

10:15.620 --> 10:16.390
Yes.

10:16.390 --> 10:20.500
I must protect Mr. Iruma 
from wicked riffraff.

10:20.500 --> 10:23.610
Though it's one thing to fend off 
those within the Kingdom of Barcula,

10:23.610 --> 10:25.040
but when it comes to other nations—

10:25.040 --> 10:28.900
especially the Holy Empire of Sidonia—
I have no idea what schemes they're plotting.

10:28.900 --> 10:30.700
I must remain vigilant.

10:31.980 --> 10:34.440
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia
Several Months After Takumi's Present Time</b>

10:37.180 --> 10:41.380
"The Goddess Anat created 
mankind in her likeness."

10:41.730 --> 10:46.420
"Afterward, she created the beastmen 
from beasts to serve mankind,"

10:46.420 --> 10:49.120
"and then she created elves 
and dwarves from sprites,"

10:49.120 --> 10:51.080
"placing them beneath mankind."

11:07.170 --> 11:10.140
So that's the Royal Capital, Bakilatos.

11:13.130 --> 11:15.730
It looks like we've arrived safely.

11:15.730 --> 11:18.470
Yeah. We didn't have any 
trouble with monsters.

11:18.470 --> 11:20.280
No trouble with monsters?

11:20.280 --> 11:22.950
Whenever any monsters did show up, 
we tried to face them,

11:22.950 --> 11:25.120
but Sofia and the others beat 
them down in a flash.

11:25.120 --> 11:29.940
Maple and that drake horse were 
practically unstoppable, too.

11:30.510 --> 11:32.700
We hardly had anything to do.

11:32.700 --> 11:35.290
You made this an awfully easy job.

11:35.290 --> 11:39.860
Mr. Takumi, once we reach the inn, 
there's something I'd like to discuss with you.

11:39.860 --> 11:40.820
Something to discuss?

11:41.900 --> 11:45.880
You're going to offer the king 
something similar to my carriage?

11:46.230 --> 11:48.790
I consulted with Lord Godwin,

11:48.790 --> 11:51.940
and he believes it's the best 
way to get His Royal Majesty

11:51.940 --> 11:54.380
to understand your exceptional talent.

11:54.380 --> 11:55.570
I see.

11:55.570 --> 11:58.250
We have our audience with 
His Majesty five days from now.

11:58.250 --> 12:01.820
I'm sure it will prove difficult 
to create one in that time frame,

12:01.820 --> 12:04.080
so you could start the work 
once we return to Bolton.

12:04.080 --> 12:04.990
I can make it in time.

12:04.990 --> 12:05.670
What?

12:05.940 --> 12:10.570
If I made it in Bolton, then we'd 
 have to haul it back here, right?

12:10.570 --> 12:14.580
Considering that effort, it would 
be better to make it right away.

12:14.580 --> 12:15.530
Oh, but...

12:15.530 --> 12:19.880
I can make do with the materials I have on hand, 
but I would need a space to use.

12:21.920 --> 12:25.430
Leave all of that to me!

12:26.370 --> 12:28.100
The Palum Company?

12:28.100 --> 12:29.220
Yeah.

12:29.220 --> 12:32.710
Papek said it's a slave trading 
company run by someone he knows.

12:32.710 --> 12:36.430
I know of it. It's owned 
by a man named Burton.

12:36.430 --> 12:39.700
The company is known to be 
trustworthy, even in the capital.

12:39.700 --> 12:41.370
That's what I heard from Mulan.

12:41.630 --> 12:44.320
They have a spacious garden in that 
detached building we can use,

12:44.320 --> 12:47.100
and Papek said he'd arrange 
for the materials, too.

12:47.100 --> 12:51.090
Um, the blueprints for the carriage are...

12:51.090 --> 12:52.590
Mr. Takumi.

12:52.590 --> 12:53.530
What is it?

12:53.530 --> 12:57.630
I believe you need someone who 
can assist with your production.

12:57.630 --> 12:58.640
Huh?

12:58.640 --> 13:01.490
You ran yourself ragged before our journey,

13:01.490 --> 13:05.250
and despite the long trip, you're starting 
production without taking a break.

13:05.250 --> 13:07.120
That's reckless, even for you, Mr. Takumi.

13:07.120 --> 13:09.640
No, I'm not particularly tired.

13:09.640 --> 13:12.270
It's fortunate that we're 
heading to the Palum Company.

13:12.270 --> 13:14.160
Why don't you try consulting with them?

13:14.410 --> 13:15.640
I have you two to help me—

13:15.640 --> 13:18.020
I can't help you with alchemy.

13:18.020 --> 13:20.320
I can only sew.

13:20.320 --> 13:21.770
Mr. Takumi.

13:21.770 --> 13:26.150
I intend to dedicate 
my life to protecting yours.

13:26.380 --> 13:30.250
I promise I will drive 
away any external threat.

13:30.250 --> 13:33.080
And I'll handle all the housework, 
even if it kills me!

13:33.280 --> 13:37.720
However, if you won't 
respect your own health,

13:37.720 --> 13:39.800
then there's nothing I can do.

13:40.340 --> 13:41.590
Sofia...

13:42.280 --> 13:44.110
Thank you, you two.

13:44.110 --> 13:45.040
I understand.

13:45.520 --> 13:47.330
Though it has to be a woman.

13:47.330 --> 13:48.710
That's important!

13:48.710 --> 13:49.920
Got it.

13:50.180 --> 13:52.640
<b>Palum Slave Trading Company</b>

13:50.730 --> 13:52.950
Are you looking for someone to contract?

13:52.950 --> 13:53.750
Yes.

13:53.750 --> 13:56.330
I'm thinking of expanding my party.

13:56.330 --> 14:00.590
If possible, I would prefer someone 
who could help with my alchemy work.

14:00.590 --> 14:06.520
I heard you were using alchemy to create 
a carriage using mythril and adamantite.

14:06.520 --> 14:07.320
Yes.

14:07.320 --> 14:10.270
In that case, you'll need 
someone with magical aptitude.

14:12.070 --> 14:13.470
Sofia!

14:13.470 --> 14:14.350
Maria?

14:14.350 --> 14:16.400
Have you seen Maple?

14:16.400 --> 14:17.420
She's not around?

14:17.420 --> 14:20.620
She was with Camellia earlier.

14:20.620 --> 14:22.890
She's not in the pocket dimension?

14:22.890 --> 14:27.380
She said she wanted to explore the
company's buildings, so I'm worried she...

14:27.380 --> 14:29.240
Went off on her own?

14:29.670 --> 14:31.510
I'll go bring her back.

14:35.300 --> 14:36.610
Maple?

14:37.090 --> 14:38.600
Maple, are you there?

14:42.090 --> 14:43.240
It's okay!

14:43.240 --> 14:44.930
I won't do anything to you!

14:44.930 --> 14:46.860
I'm just exploring right now!

14:46.860 --> 14:47.810
Maple!

14:47.810 --> 14:49.200
Sofia!

14:49.200 --> 14:50.620
What are you doing?

14:50.620 --> 14:52.480
Don't go wandering off on your own.

14:52.480 --> 14:53.520
Fine.

14:53.520 --> 14:54.970
I'm sorry.

14:54.970 --> 14:55.980
Are you alright?

14:55.980 --> 14:57.560
Y-Yes.

14:58.120 --> 14:59.600
She's not dangerous.

14:59.600 --> 15:00.840
She's a good girl.

15:01.890 --> 15:05.420
Y-Yes, I'm just startled.

15:08.880 --> 15:11.130
This looks like an ancient book.

15:11.130 --> 15:12.960
Yes. It's an old one from the library.

15:12.960 --> 15:16.920
There are a lot of unwanted 
books on magic here.

15:16.920 --> 15:20.810
This one is <i>The Encyclopedia on the 
Fundamentals of Arnold-Style Alchemy</i>.

15:20.810 --> 15:22.310
Alchemy?

15:22.310 --> 15:24.580
They say alchemy circles are old-fashioned,

15:24.580 --> 15:28.970
but this is absolutely the best way to learn 
the basics of decomposition and recomposition!

15:31.060 --> 15:32.630
Oh, Sofia.

15:32.940 --> 15:35.020
I was just thinking of calling for you.

15:35.020 --> 15:36.410
For me?

15:36.410 --> 15:39.020
I'm on my way to meet a candidate,

15:39.020 --> 15:41.210
but I was wondering if 
you would accompany me.

15:44.750 --> 15:46.590
Pardon me!

15:49.660 --> 15:52.040
This is Mr. Takumi Iruma.

15:52.040 --> 15:54.990
He works as a producer in Bolton.

15:54.990 --> 15:56.730
N-Nice to meet you!

15:56.730 --> 15:58.100
My name is Reyva!

15:58.100 --> 15:59.150
Hello.

16:04.870 --> 16:08.970
I also do some adventuring in 
addition to my production work,

16:08.970 --> 16:10.060
<i>What should I do?</i>

16:08.970 --> 16:11.110
but that's mainly to 
maintain my status.

16:10.060 --> 16:11.830
<i>If I don't get accepted this time either,</i>

16:12.180 --> 16:14.800
<i>then I won't be able to do 
anything for my family.</i>

16:12.920 --> 16:16.440
I mainly use magic for my production.

16:16.440 --> 16:20.540
I'd be happy if you have any 
knowledge or interest in alchemy.

16:20.910 --> 16:22.530
A-Alchemy?!

16:22.530 --> 16:23.900
Y-Yes!

16:23.900 --> 16:25.390
Are you interested in it?

16:26.040 --> 16:28.250
But what can you do with it?

16:28.250 --> 16:34.980
I don't intend to take care of you for the 
time it takes you to learn something useful.

16:38.290 --> 16:39.580
Reyva...

16:40.700 --> 16:41.890
Mr. Takumi.

16:42.710 --> 16:46.850
It appears she's been studying and learning 
many different types of magic on her own here.

16:46.850 --> 16:48.430
You have?

16:48.720 --> 16:52.250
Amongst those was a book on alchemy.

16:52.250 --> 16:54.900
I believe it was, uh, A-Arn—

16:54.900 --> 16:57.970
<i>The Encyclopedia on the Fundamentals 
of Arnold-Style Alchemy!</i>

16:59.000 --> 17:01.570
Wow, not Arron Martin then?

17:01.820 --> 17:02.480
Yes!

17:02.480 --> 17:05.510
Arron is often seen as the 
foundational book for alchemy,

17:05.510 --> 17:08.670
but I believe it's derived 
from the Arnold style!

17:08.670 --> 17:10.050
I knew it!

17:10.050 --> 17:12.380
It does feel like he's summarizing 
Arnold's work, doesn't it?

17:12.380 --> 17:15.580
It's understandable the more recent 
publication would receive attention,

17:15.580 --> 17:18.670
but I don't think we should 
forget the founding principles!

17:18.670 --> 17:20.650
<i>Two birds of a feather?</i>

17:18.670 --> 17:20.650
The foundations are 
important, aren't they!

17:20.650 --> 17:22.230
In that case...

17:25.100 --> 17:26.680
Look at this.

17:26.680 --> 17:29.080
Can you tell what this 
alchemy circle is for?

17:30.950 --> 17:33.580
<i>Recomposition of a specific material?</i>

17:34.000 --> 17:36.620
<i>With heating and shape alteration?</i>

17:41.420 --> 17:47.340
<i>It's similar to the alchemy circle for spiraling
sweets, but it's not using Candy Bee honey?</i>

17:48.880 --> 17:50.390
<i>Something's different.</i>

17:51.890 --> 17:54.520
<i>I have to do my best... 
I </i>have<i> to do my best...</i>

17:54.790 --> 17:57.960
<i>I have to figure it out,
or I'll be rejected again.</i>

17:58.600 --> 18:00.160
<i>Even if I have to...</i>

18:00.810 --> 18:02.980
<i>fake it...</i>

18:07.770 --> 18:10.740
I don't know.

18:12.260 --> 18:16.790
In my hometown, 
we don't use fluffy cream,

18:17.910 --> 18:20.590
we use Candy Bee honey.

18:21.940 --> 18:24.810
<i>Of course I'll be rejected, again.</i>

18:32.540 --> 18:34.940
I would love to have you.

18:35.450 --> 18:36.460
Huh?

18:38.280 --> 18:43.230
I'd like to have you accompany us when 
we adventure, helping as my assistant.

18:43.230 --> 18:44.990
But I won't force you.

18:44.990 --> 18:46.510
P-Please, hold on!

18:46.840 --> 18:49.550
I didn't figure out your alchemy circle!

18:49.550 --> 18:52.490
It was nothing like the one 
I know for spiraling sweets.

18:52.490 --> 18:56.330
Yeah, but it <i>is</i> an alchemy circle 
for one of those spiraling sweets.

18:56.330 --> 18:57.320
Huh?!

18:57.320 --> 19:01.450
I knew that different regions paired 
different things with the dough,

19:01.900 --> 19:05.000
but yeah, using honey does sound delicious!

19:05.000 --> 19:06.490
Y-Yes!

19:06.490 --> 19:10.200
I rarely got a chance to eat it, 
but my little brother loves it!

19:10.200 --> 19:13.450
You were able to quickly 
understand it at a glance.

19:13.450 --> 19:15.830
It's not like you can't use alchemy at all.

19:15.830 --> 19:17.950
Th-Then I'm...

19:17.950 --> 19:20.180
Yeah. Nice to have you, Reyva!

19:24.890 --> 19:28.380
I'll work as hard as possible!

19:28.380 --> 19:30.330
I look forward to working with you!

19:36.700 --> 19:38.850
The contract is complete.

19:38.850 --> 19:44.540
For compensation, are you okay with daily wages
and potential raises based on your abilities?

19:44.540 --> 19:45.940
U-Um...

19:45.940 --> 19:50.110
Could you please have all my 
wages sent back to my home?

19:50.110 --> 19:52.910
I don't mind that, but...
 do you mean all of your wages?

19:52.910 --> 19:56.380
The village I'm from is very poor.

19:56.380 --> 20:00.990
I left my family with some money 
by becoming a debt slave,

20:00.990 --> 20:04.140
but that won't last forever.

20:04.990 --> 20:08.170
I don't want my little 
brother to live in poverty.

20:08.170 --> 20:13.680
I want him to go to school, and I want 
to help make life easier for my mother.

20:13.680 --> 20:14.530
But...

20:14.530 --> 20:18.270
If we send all of it, then 
you'll remain a slave forever.

20:18.270 --> 20:20.370
I think you should accept her request.

20:20.370 --> 20:21.610
Sofia?

20:21.610 --> 20:26.180
Once she learns more techniques—
including alchemy—under you,

20:26.180 --> 20:30.360
she'll be able to earn her living from
her own capabilities one day.

20:30.360 --> 20:34.710
Besides, serving under your 
contracted master forever

20:34.710 --> 20:36.580
can be one form of happiness.

20:36.580 --> 20:40.320
Especially when you have 
 a wonderful master.

20:40.930 --> 20:42.260
Alright.

20:42.260 --> 20:43.960
If you say so.

20:45.050 --> 20:47.760
Yay!

20:47.760 --> 20:49.970
Hey now, don't charge her!

20:49.970 --> 20:51.020
Welcome, newbie!

20:51.020 --> 20:52.360
You're intensely welcome here!

20:52.360 --> 20:54.270
I-I'm Reyva!

20:54.270 --> 20:55.580
I'm Maple!

20:55.580 --> 20:57.330
This girl is Camellia!

20:57.330 --> 20:58.500
I'm Maria!

20:58.500 --> 21:00.420
Leave all the housework to me!

21:00.420 --> 21:02.830
Huh? Are you all going to talk like her now?

21:02.830 --> 21:04.350
That's right!

21:03.440 --> 21:04.730
That's right!

21:04.730 --> 21:06.890
I think it's cute, Mr. Takumi!

21:04.730 --> 21:07.610
<i>I think I'll be able to work hard with them.</i>

21:09.030 --> 21:14.000
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia, Present</b>

21:10.240 --> 21:14.010
The Kingdom of Barcula's 
attitude hasn't changed?

21:14.010 --> 21:16.290
We've sent them missives three times,

21:16.290 --> 21:19.920
and they insist on refusing, like 
they're stamping out the same reply.

21:20.680 --> 21:26.170
In that case, we'll need to teach them a lesson,
 even if it means getting a little rough.

21:26.170 --> 21:27.250
As you wish!

21:27.250 --> 21:29.680
I'll assemble the knights at once.

21:29.680 --> 21:31.750
Please wait, Father.

21:32.510 --> 21:37.220
It won't be long until our
nation summons the heroes.

21:37.220 --> 21:40.940
I think we should avoid any hasty 
action these next few months.

21:40.940 --> 21:44.320
Though we cannot leave this unaddressed.

21:44.320 --> 21:46.900
This is precisely the time 
for the power of faith.

21:47.520 --> 21:50.180
You would use our faithful?

21:50.180 --> 21:51.980
I wouldn't say use.

21:51.980 --> 21:56.540
We simply spread word that there's someone 
disrespecting the Church of Divine Light.

21:56.900 --> 21:58.380
I see.

21:58.380 --> 22:02.090
That would incite the 
anger of our believers.

22:03.180 --> 22:08.410
And when that happens, the Divine Light 
Squadron won't remain silent on the matter.
